The code statements that fix the bug are:
mutex_lock(&ctx->walk_control_lock);
if (ctx->walk_control == control)
    ctx->walk_control = NULL;
mutex_unlock(&ctx->walk_control_lock);
Reason: Before returning -EINVAL, the fix acquires the lock and clears the pointer (if it still points to the same control), preventing the dangling pointer while ensuring thread safety.

